{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>אשת.</b> Even a married woman." "<b>ולקחת לך לאשה.</b> The Torah spoke only against the evil inclination — for if the Holy One, blessed be He, does not permit her to him, he will marry her in prohibition. But if he does marry her, his end will be to hate her, as it is stated immediately after: ״כִּי תִהְיֶיןָ לְאִישׁ וגו׳״, and his end will be to father from her a wayward and rebellious son. Therefore these passages are juxtaposed (Tanchuma)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:51.611210653Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}